# Architecture Rules

These constraints are testable. Each rule names a specific, verifiable condition.

- No file in `src/` may import `zustand`, `redux`, `@reduxjs/toolkit`, or `react-context` — state is prop-drilled from `App.jsx`
- No component file may call `localStorage` directly — all storage access must go through `useStorage`, `useRecipes`, or `usePrefs` (verify: `grep -r 'localStorage' src/components/`)
- Every function exported from `src/utils/` must be pure: no `localStorage`, no `fetch`, no `useEffect`, no side effects (verify: `grep -r 'localStorage\|fetch\|useEffect' src/utils/`)
- Every interactive element must be a `<button>` element — `<div onClick>` and `<span onClick>` are forbidden (verify: `grep -rn 'onClick' src/components/ | grep -v '<button'`)
- No file in `src/` may exceed 500 lines — warn at 400, CI hard-fails new/modified files at 650
